se_id":"toolu_01VLkTtbdZ2BpCRruxCjeqvD"},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"curl -s -H \"Authorization: Bearer ${PAPERCLIP_API_KEY}\" \"${PAPERCLIP_API_URL}/api/agents/me\"","description":"Fetch my Paperclip agent identity"},"tool_use_id":"toolu_0166rGuDGfJjzqsApkyszNCL"},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"echo \"API_URL=$PAPERCLIP_API_URL AGENT_ID=$PAPERCLIP_AGENT_ID COMPANY_ID=$PAPERCLIP_COMPANY_ID RUN_ID=$PAPERCLIP_RUN_ID TASK_ID=$PAPERCLIP_TASK_ID WAKE_REASON=$PAPERCLIP_WAKE_REASON WAKE_COMMENT=$PAPERCLIP_WAKE_COMMENT_ID\"","description":"Print Paperclip env vars"},"tool_use_id":"toolu_01382TGJENkqxpqGrHixwaf9"},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"printenv | grep PAPERCLIP","description":"List Paperclip environment variables"},"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TyfWUCXNJRGuwx45eiNox9"},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"env | grep PAPERCLIP","description":"Show Paperclip environment variables"},"tool_use_id":"toolu_016sReWgrUEB25nsb2CFz1w8"},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"echo $PAPERCLIP_API_URL","description":"Get API URL"},"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WHhKTfmxiqm3SY5jjLMCRc"},{"tool_name":"AskUserQuestion","tool_input":{"questions":[{"header":"Permissions","options":[{"label":"Approve shell access","description":"Allow me to run curl and echo commands to interact with the Paperclip API"},{"label":"Skip for now","description":"Exit this heartbeat without doing work"}],"question":"My bash commands are being blocked by permissions. Could you approve shell access so I can call the Paperclip API (curl commands to check my identity and inbox)?","multiSelect":false}]},"tool_use_id":"toolu_01V9rq4af7rW7DpqvfXspwL7"}]}$paperclip$, NULL, $paperclip$7b223429-9faf-41d8-b4f3-f60ae9697c5b$paperclip$, $paperclip$local_file$paperclip$, $paperclip$5022ffc0-de8b-45b2-89c6-38f62fcdee32/bcdca989-a17d-4e9a-9a9d-fe9144cbfd64/1f07e053-4a99-4a88-ad09-b75a59157379.ndjson$paperclip$, $paperclip$67059$paperclip$, $paperclip$6964d5d9c934a83c58d165136b3beaa562111dc6bfdeac76ec37b9009976ee5b$paperclip$, false, $paperclip$ CEO agents may use the safe routes with `target.mode = \"new_company\"` to create a new company directly. Paperclip copies active user memberships from the source company so the new company is not orphaned.\n\nFor export, preview first and keep tasks explicit:\n\n- `POST /api/companies/{companyId}/exports/preview`\n- `POST /api/companies/{companyId}/exports`\n- Export preview defaults to `issues: false`\n- Add `issues` or `projectIssues` only when you intentionally need task files\n- Use `selectedFiles` to narrow the final package to specific agents, skills, projects, or tasks after you inspect the preview inventory\n\n## Searching Issues\n\nUse the `q` query parameter on the issues list endpoint to search across titles, identifiers, descriptions, and comments:\n\n```\nGET /api/companies/{companyId}/issues?q=dockerfile\n```\n\nResults are ranked by relevance: title matches first, then identifier, description, and comments. You can combine `q` with other filters (`status`, `assigneeAgentId`, `projectId`, `labelId`).\n\n## Self-Test Playbook (App-Level)\n\nUse this when validating Paperclip itself (assignment flow, checkouts, run visibility, and status transitions).\n\n1. Create a throwaway issue assigned to a known local agent (`claudecoder` or `codexcoder`):\n\n```bash\nnpx paperclipai issue create \\\n  --company-id \"$PAPERCLIP_COMPANY_ID\" \\\n  --title \"Self-test: assignment/watch flow\" \\\n  --description \"Temporary validation issue\" \\\n  --status todo \\\n  --assignee-agent-id \"$PAPERCLIP_AGENT_ID\"\n```\n\n2. Trigger and watch a heartbeat for that assignee:\n\n```bash\nnpx paperclipai heartbeat run --agent-id \"$PAPERCLIP_AGENT_ID\"\n```\n\n3. Verify the issue transitions (`todo -> in_progress -> done` or `blocked`) and that comments are posted:\n\n```bash\nnpx paperclipai issue get <issue-id-or-identifier>\n```\n\n4. Reassignment test (optional): move the same issue between `claudecoder` and `codexcoder` and confirm wake/run behavior:\n\n```bash\nnpx paperclipai issue update <issue-id> --assignee-agent-id <other-agent-id> --status todo\n```\n\n5. Cleanup: mark temporary issues done/cancelled with a clear note.\n\nIf you use direct `curl` during these tests, include `X-Paperclip-Run-Id` on all mutating issue requests whenever running inside a heartbeat.\n\n## Full Reference\n\nFor detailed API tables, JSON response schemas, worked examples (IC and Manager heartbeats), governance/approvals, cross-team delegation rules, error codes, issue lifecycle diagram, and the common mistakes table, read: `skills/paperclip/references/api-reference.md`\n\n\nARGUMENTS: Check my current assignments and any pending tasks"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b223429-9faf-41d8-b4f3-f60ae9697c5b","uuid":"ffcf8161-7080-4e73-9ad5-2f5211106118","timestamp":"2026-04-03T21:42:09.375Z","isSynthetic":true}
